<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Canberra extends ASC deputy chair appointment.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Canberra extends ASC deputy chair appointment.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government announced on Thursday it had extended the appointment of Lynn Ralph as deputy chairman of the Australian Securities Commission (ASC) until the end of March next year.</p>
<p>Ralph joined the ASC in October 1993 and since then has been responsible for the &quot;Good Advice&quot; report which deals with improving regulation of Australian investment advisory services.</p>
<p>The extension of Ralph's appointment would allow her to continue her current work on making prospectuses more simple and more accessible to the Australian public, the government said in a statement.   -- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273 2730</p>
